        "texto": "Among people of pastoral and nomadic habits it is natural to estimate wealth, not by houses and lands, but by the number of animals owned. Abram was very rich in cattle (Gen. 13:2). Lot had flocks and herds (Gen. 13:5). See also Genesis 24:35. Job’s wealth, on the return of his p…",
